# Beta-1 National Waste Movements

Beta-1 is the National Waste Movements API (collections). Tests live in `test/specs/WasteMovementExternalAPI/beta-1/`. The version folder is kebab-case. Behavior files sit directly in it (for example `create-collection.test.js`).

## Client and data

- Call `globalThis.apis.wasteMovementExternalAPI.beta1`
- Build payloads with the `beta1` generators in `test/support/test-data-manager.js`:
  - `generateBaseMovementData()` for `POST /beta-1/movements`
  - `generateBaseCollectionData()` for `POST /beta-1/movements/{movementId}/collection`
  - `generateBaseDeliveryData(movementIds)` for `POST /beta-1/deliveries`
  - `generateBaseReceiptData()` for `POST /beta-1/deliveries/{deliveryId}/receipt`
  - `generateBaseReceiptWithoutDeliveryIdData()` for `POST /beta-1/receipts`
- Payloads include the run-scoped `apiCode` (`API_CODE` from global setup, exposed as `globalThis.testConfig.apiCode`). Do not invent an API code inside a test
- Use `beta1.unknownResourceId` for a well-formed ID that does not exist

## Lifecycle

A later step needs the IDs from earlier steps in the same test:

1. Create a movement and read `movementId`
2. Record a collection against that movement
3. Record a delivery with those movement IDs and read `deliveryId`
4. Record a receipt against the delivery, or a receipt without a delivery ID

## Problem responses

Assert the status code first. Assert `response.headers['x-request-id']` with `expect.any(String)`. Then `toEqual()` the problem body:

- `type`: `https://defra.github.io/digital-waste-tracking-api-docs/preview/problems/` plus `bad-request` or `not-found`
- `title`, `detail`, `instance`
- `requestId`: `response.headers['x-request-id']`

Receipt validation errors (`key`, `errorType`, `message`) do not apply to these endpoints.
